# Cloudflare Pages quirks this file has to live with (doc/redirects_en.md):
#   - A wildcard rewrite takes precedence over the static asset tree. A rule
#     like `/products/* / 200` shadows EVERY prerendered page under that prefix
#     with the homepage shell. Verified live 2026-10-21: 255 of 269 sitemap
#     URLs were serving the homepage title and a homepage canonical, because
#     the prefix block below used to exist. Only exact rules for paths that
#     have no prerendered sibling are safe — Pages will not warn you.
#   - A wildcard rule whose target is "/index.html" is dropped in silence:
#     Pages exposes the root document as "/", so that target never resolves.
#   - An EXACT rule whose target is "/index.html" is NOT dropped — it fires and
#     308-redirects to "/", silently losing the path. Verified live 2026-10-21:
#     the bare roots were written that way and /compare answered 308 -> /
#     while /compare/ answered 404. "/index.html" is never a valid target;
#     target "/" (a rewrite serves the shell at the original URL).
#   - An exact source matches ONLY the form written: "/compare" does not cover
#     "/compare/". Both forms need their own rule (verified live 2026-10-21 —
#     the no-slash rule left the slash form 404ing).
#   - Pages rejects the "200!" suffix as an invalid status code.
#   - Rules match top-down, the file is capped (~120 lines), and the overflow
#     is dropped without failing the build.
# Retired-URL 301s do NOT live here: that family is owned by the Worker
# (backend/api/worker/src/legacyRedirects.generated.ts, mirrored from
# dist/data/legacy-redirects.json by front/scripts/sync_redirects_to_worker.mjs).
# A fallback for unknown sub-paths is not expressible here at all — a wildcard
# cannot be made to lose to a static file. Guard: npm run check:redirects.

/api/* https://store.balancebiketoddler.com/api/:splat 307

# Bare app roots: SPA-only routes with no prerendered sibling, so the shell
# needs an explicit exact rewrite. Do NOT widen these to wildcards — that is
# the shape that shadowed 255 prerendered pages (see the precedence note above).
# Both URL forms get their own rule: Pages matches the source exactly, so
# "/compare" alone leaves "/compare/" on the 404 page. Target "/", never
# "/index.html" (see the 308 note above). Guard: npm run check:redirects.
/compare / 200
/compare/ / 200
/auth / 200
/auth/ / 200
/search / 200
/search/ / 200
/transparency / 200
/transparency/ / 200
